      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Very interesting race. If this was at Moonee Valley there's almost no doubt JIGSAW (2) would be a clear favourite but the straight is something he hasn't seen in a long time. He's 0/4 at Flemington with two of those down the straight but it's tough to judge him on old form - he's unbeaten in his past eight and going better than ever. Perhaps the straight factor will be overplayed. EXTRAGALACTIC (8) is yet to see the straight but does profile as a horse that would enjoy it given her big turn of foot. She's been excellent in the Moir & Manikato this time in and will be rattling home under J-Mac. SMOOTH CHINO (5) was a strange watch here in the G2 Gilgai. Both Galati & Ben Melham stopped riding before the post in a close finish. Not sure he'd have won that but he can only improve for the experience. REY MAGNERIO (3) was okay behind JIGSAW fresh and can improve here. MAZU (1) beat Joliestar fresh albeit with a very soft lead, he'll run well up on top of the speed.",
